    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Meetup API Event Fetcher\n\n## This workflow uses the OFFICIAL Meetup API\n\n### Benefits over HTTP Scraping:\n✅ No anti-bot issues\n✅ Structured JSON data\n✅ Proper pagination\n✅ Location-based search built-in\n✅ Topic filtering\n✅ Legal and supported\n✅ Faster and more reliable\n\n### Requirements:\n1. Meetup API Key (free tier available)\n   - Go to: https://www.meetup.com/api/\n   - Create an OAuth consumer\n   - Get your API key\n\n2. Configure credentials in n8n:\n   - Go to Credentials\n   - Add HTTP Header Auth\n   - Name: Authorization\n   - Value: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\n\n### Google Sheet Structure:\n\n**Tab 1: Locations**\n- location: City name (e.g., \"San Francisco\")\n- latitude: Lat coordinate (e.g., 37.7749)\n- longitude: Lon coordinate (e.g., -122.4194)\n- radius: Search radius in miles (e.g., 25)\n\n**Tab 2: Topics**\n- topic: Topic name that maps to Meetup category\n  - technology, ai, machine learning\n  - software, programming\n  - blockchain, cryptocurrency\n  - fitness, health\n  - arts, music\n  - etc.\n\n**Tab 3: Results (auto-filled)**\nAll event data including:\n- Event name, URL, date\n- Group info and member count\n- Venue and location details\n- RSVP counts and status\n- Description preview\n\n### Rate Limits:\n- 100 requests per minute (free tier)\n- Workflow includes 1-second delay\n- For heavy usage, increase delay",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -280,
        40
      ],
